'''''Heterodactylus lundii''''', also known [[Common name|commonly]] as '''Lund's teiid''', is an [[Endangered species|endangered]] [[species]] of [[lizard]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Gymnophthalmidae]].<ref name=RDB>{{NRDB species |genus=Heterodactylus |species=lundii |accessdate=27 July 2019}}</ref> The species is [[Endemism|endemic]] to [[Brazil]].

==Etymology==
The [[Specific name (zoology)|specific name]], ''lundii'', is in honor of Danish [[Paleontology|paleontologist]] [[Peter Wilhelm Lund]].<ref>[[Bo Beolens|Beolens, Bo]]; [[Michael Watkins (zoologist)|Watkins, Michael]]; [[Michael Grayson|Grayson, Michael]] (2011). ''The Eponym Dictionary of Reptiles''. Baltimore: Johns Hopkins University Press. xiii + 296 pp. {{ISBN|978-1-4214-0135-5}}. (''Heterodactylus lundii'', pp. 162–163).</ref>

==Description==
''Heterodactylus lundii'' has an elongated body and very small legs. It may attain a [[Snout–vent length|snout-to-vent length]] (SVL) of {{cvt|6|cm|in}}. The tail length is about twice the SVL.<ref name=iucn/>

==Geographic range==
''Heterodactylus lundii'' is found in the Brazilian state of [[Minas Gerais]].<ref name=iucn/><ref name=RDB/>

==Habitat==
The preferred natural [[habitat]] of ''Heterodactylus lundii'' is [[savanna]], at altitudes of {{cvt|900|–|1,300|m|ft}}.<ref name=iucn/>

==Behavior==
''Heterodactylus lundii'' is [[Terrestrial locomotion|terrestrial]] and [[fossorial]].<ref name=iucn/>

==Reproduction==
''Heterodactylus lundii'' is [[Oviparity|oviparous]].<ref name=iucn/><ref name=RDB/> [[Clutch (eggs)|Clutch]] size is only two eggs.<ref name=iucn/>

